# SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-S-2.0
#
# tile_up5k_board.pcf -- BOARD/production pin map for the UP5K fallback board
# (iCE40UP5K-SG48I, SG48 = QFN48 7x7 mm, 0.5 mm pitch, GND paddle).
#
# Every pin verified against the Lattice primary pinout file fetched
# 2026-10-12 from the Lattice product page (document_id=51971, "# Pin Out
# For iCE5UP5K" Rev 1.1, F column = SG48; see ../data/pins_ice40up_sg48.json
# for provenance + sha256) plus FPGA-DS-02008-2.4 (rails, POR, power-up
# sequence) and FPGA-TN-02001-3.5 (boot selection, CRESET_B pure input).
# The empirical chipdb census (pads missing {1,5,7,8,22,24,29,30,33} =
# {VCCIO2,VCC,CDONE,CRESET_B,SPI_VCCIO1,VPP_2V5,VCCPLL,VCC,VCCIO0}) matches
# the vendor map EXACTLY - no inference from tool behaviour anywhere here.
#
# RESERVED (never tile IO): 7 CDONE, 8 CRESET_B, 14 SPI_SO, 15 SPI_SCK,
# 16 SPI_SS, 17 SPI_SI (the four SPI config pads route to the external config
# flash + in-circuit programming test pads), 39/40/41 RGB LED drivers
# (excluded: open-drain LED outputs, no-LED user rule), power pins
# 1,5,22,24,29,30,33 + paddle GND.
#
# iCE40 pads: pull-UP only -> the rev-A pull-DOWN inputs get PAD pull-ups
# ONLY for the UP class; the DOWN class (t_data, l_data, b_latch, r_latch)
# and all 12 keys carry external 10K pull-down resistors on the board
# (BOM delta +16 x 10K vs the GW1NZ variant; see docs/power_reg.md).
# clk on IOT_46b_G0 (GBIN): the choice gives the merged 20 MHz clock a
# direct global buffer path.

# 12 keys (switch to VCC + EXTERNAL 10K pull-down each; no pad pull set)
set_io keys[0] 2
set_io keys[1] 3
set_io keys[2] 4
set_io keys[3] 9
set_io keys[4] 10
set_io keys[5] 11
set_io keys[6] 12
set_io keys[7] 13
set_io keys[8] 18
set_io keys[9] 19
set_io keys[10] 20
set_io keys[11] 44

# merged 20 MHz shift clock (J103.2 = J104.2) on the GBIN pad
set_io -pullup yes clk_pin 35

# rev-A pull-UP strap inputs
set_io -pullup yes t_w_pin 23
set_io -pullup yes t_endcol_pin 25
set_io -pullup yes b_first_pin 26
set_io -pullup yes l_endrow_pin 27

# rev-A pull-DOWN inputs (external 10K on the board; no pad pull set)
set_io t_data_pin 28
set_io l_data_pin 31
set_io b_latch_pin 32
set_io r_latch_pin 34

# outputs (t_clk/l_clk are true tri-state SB_IO, verified by the fpga flow)
set_io t_clk_pin 36
set_io l_clk_pin 37
set_io latcho_pin 38
set_io dout_pin 42
set_io b_w_pin 43
